      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s findstring, but it does not matter which function it is. Here\u0027s the makefile (/tmp/sp.mk):\n```\n$(info filter\u003d$(filter a,a b #))\n$(info sort\u003d$(sort b #a))\nifdef ASSIGN\n#Z:\u003d$(sort a #b)\nZ:\u003d$(filter a,a # b)\nendif\nall:\n```\n\n$ make -f /tmp/sp.mk\nfilter\u003da\nsort\u003d#a b\nmake: Nothing to be done for \u0027all\u0027.\n$ make -f /tmp/sp.mk ASSIGN\u003da\nfilter\u003da\nsort\u003d#a b\n/tmp/sp.mk:4: *** unterminated call to function \u0027sort\u0027: missing \u0027)\u0027.  Stop.\n\n\nLooks like assignments are treated differently.",
